      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The common myna is an Asian invasive species in Israel. Mynas escaped
    captivity in the late 1990s and spread rapidly across the country.


    Their
    presence severely damages local wildlife. Mynas fiercely compete with native
    birds for food and nesting spaces. They steal tree holes from species like the
    house sparrow.


    Mynas also hunt directly. They destroy nests and eat the
    eggs and chicks of native birds. This aggression reduces breeding populations
    and pushes local wildlife out of their habitats.


    The hoopoe and our other
    birds may win in the game, but in real life, they lost a long time ago.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
